The dummies \code{uk}, \code{germany} and \code{usa} sum to 1 in every row, so a model with
an intercept can include only two of them, and the one left out is the
reference; \code{factor(country)} makes Germany (\code{"276"}) the reference.
\code{reading} is the PISA proficiency level (0 = below level 1, up to 5),
